-- title:
--   Descending level automorphisms along a coefficient embedding
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime, $M'$ a nonzero natural number with $q \nmid M'$, and $\ell$ a prime with $\ell \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and $\ell \mid M'$. Let $L_0$ be a field of characteristic zero which is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of order $q\ell$, let $\xi_0 \in L_0$ be a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity, let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero and $\iota_0 : L_0 \to L$ a ring homomorphism, and assume there is a ring homomorphism $\iota : L \to \mathbb{C}$ with $\iota(\iota_0 \xi_0) = e^{2\pi i/(q\ell)}$. Let $H_1 \le (\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times$ be the intersection of [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH q M'`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelJacobian.html#L22), the kernel of reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$, with the kernel of reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/\ell)^\times$. Let $K_0$ (respectively $K$) be [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103) of the $q$-expansion function field [`ModularCurve.xHFunctionField (q ^ 2 * M') H₁`](def/ModularCurve_XH.html#L79) over $L_0$ (respectively $L$), that is, the intermediate field of $L_0((X))$ over $L_0$ generated by the image of that field of rational Laurent expansions under the coefficient embedding $\mathbb{Q} \to L_0$ (respectively $\mathbb{Q} \to L$). The conclusion has two parts. First, applying [`ModularCurve.coeffMap ι₀`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L16) coefficientwise to the Laurent series underlying any element of $K_0$ gives an element of $K$. Second, for every $\gamma \in \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ lying in $\Gamma_0(M')$ and every $L$-algebra automorphism $\tau$ of $K$ satisfying `IsLevelAutAt L q ((ι₀ ξ₀) ^ ℓ) q (q ^ 2 * M') H₁ γ⁻¹ K τ`, there is an $L_0$-algebra automorphism $\tau_0$ of $K_0$ satisfying the corresponding predicate `IsLevelAutAt L₀ q (ξ₀ ^ ℓ) q (q ^ 2 * M') H₁ γ⁻¹ K₀ τ₀` such that $\tau$ of the coefficientwise image of $x$ equals the coefficientwise image of $\tau_0 x$, for every $x \in K_0$. Here `IsLevelAutAt L n ζ m N₀ H δ K τ` asserts that for every weight $k \in \mathbb{Z}$, every pair $f, g$ of modular forms of weight $k$ on the image of $\Gamma_H(N_0)$ in $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{R})$, every pair of integral power series whose images in $\mathbb{C}[[X]]$ are the $q$-expansions of $f$ and $g$, with the series attached to $g$ nonzero over $\mathbb{Q}$, every $x \in K$ whose Laurent series is the image of the quotient of those two series under the coefficient embedding $\mathbb{Q} \to L$, and every ring homomorphism $\iota : L \to \mathbb{C}$ with $\iota \zeta = e^{2\pi i/n}$, the coefficientwise image of $\tau x$ under $\iota$, times the $q$-expansion of $g \mid_k \mathrm{conjElemN}\, m\, \delta$, equals the $q$-expansion of $f \mid_k \mathrm{conjElemN}\, m\, \delta$, where $\mathrm{conjElemN}\, m\, \delta$ is the matrix $\begin{pmatrix} a & b/m \\ mc & d\end{pmatrix}$ attached to $\delta = \begin{pmatrix} a & b \\ c & d\end{pmatrix}$.
--
--   This is the descent step for the automorphisms attached to $\Gamma_0(M')$-classes: an automorphism of the $L$-base change of the function field of the modular curve of level $H_1$ inside $q^2M'$, characterised by its effect on quotients of $q$-expansions of modular forms, is shown to come from an automorphism already defined over the cyclotomic field $L_0 = \mathbb{Q}(\xi_0)$, compatibly with the coefficient map induced by $\iota_0$. Existence of the automorphism over $L_0$ rests on [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_isLevelAutAt_of_mem_gamma0_of_eq_levelH_inf_ker`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_isLevelAutAt_of_mem_gamma0_of_eq_levelH_inf_ker), and the result feeds the construction of the completed local rings at the cusps of the base-changed Drinfeld charts and the comparison of level automorphisms with the diamond-operator rigid data.
